    "Book card N": 4,
    "Text": "1. ARCHETYPE AND SYMBOLISM\nThe Four of Cups is the card of marriage and family, symbolizing stability, security and satisfaction in partnership and friendship relationships. Known as the “wedding card”, it carries the energy of high ideals, romantic dreams and the pursuit of harmony with loved ones.\nCard number: 4\n\n2. STRENGTHS\nPeople with this card are wonderful protectors and healers who intuitively sense who needs help and support. They are kind, sincere, generous and know how to show sympathy. They have high intelligence, a scientific way of thinking and the ability to manage finances. They often succeed as teachers or group leaders, thanks to their ability to work with people.\n\n3. CHALLENGES\nThe main weakness is the tendency to despotism and excessive control over family, friends and colleagues, caused by the fear of losing their security. This aspiration can repel loved ones who seek independence. They are prone to self-criticism in physical and emotional terms, which leads to low self-esteem and health problems. When reality does not meet their high ideals, they can fall into despair.\n\n4. LOVE AND RELATIONSHIPS\n\nIn love, they are loving and devoted spouses who adhere to high romantic standards. They look for people of their own \"color\", but must learn to give their partner freedom, instead of limiting him out of fear. Four of Cups men attract women of the Spade suit, but build the best relationships with Spathia women. Women with this card are extremely suitable partners for Spathia men.\n\n5. WORK AND MONEY\n\nProfessional success comes when they choose one direction of activity and follow it to the end. They are suitable for teachers, doctors, social workers or financial experts. They have a sense of money and strive for a high professional position, but they must be careful with the temptations of power. Their well-being depends on their ability to take real, rather than ostentatious, care for people.\n\n6. KARMIC LESSON\nThe main spiritual task is to free themselves from the habit of controlling others and to understand that not everyone needs their protection. They must overcome the fear of losing stability and realize that true security comes from unconditional love and trust, and not from imposing power over others.\n\n7. LIFE CYCLES\nMercury (0-13 years): A period of early awareness of the value of money, a desire to earn and save.\nVenus (13-26 years): A time for fruitful cooperation with people who are close in spirit and interests.\nMars (26-39 years): Building popularity and authority among friends and colleagues.\nJupiter (39-52 years): Acquisition of new knowledge and activation of rich intuition.\nSaturn (52+ years): Period of stability, stagnation or preservation of the achieved favorable position."
