    "Text": "1. ARCHETYPE AND SYMBOLISM\nThe Two of Cups is the card of love, heartfelt union, and intimate partnership. It belongs to the “semi-fixed” cards and symbolizes the need for communication, sharing, and deep affection between two people, whether they are lovers or close friends.\nCard number: 2\n\n2. STRENGTHS\nThose born with this card have a strong will, confidence in their actions, and do not like to be led. They are gifted with an excellent analytical mind, insatiable curiosity, and intellectual potential. They often have a talent for metaphysics and can be good mediums. They are successful in material well-being and business, demonstrating practicality and exactingness.\n\n3. CHALLENGES\nTheir main fear is loneliness, which can make them want to be with someone at any cost, or vice versa – in case of severe disappointment, completely isolate themselves. They are prone to too high idealism and fantasies in love, which are shattered in reality. They often approach feelings too intellectually. Fears about their financial situation can undermine their health.\n\n4. LOVE AND RELATIONSHIPS\nFor them, partnership is vital and they have a hard time living alone; they are looking for the “one” and are ready to wait a long time. They have a strong karmic connection with the Ace of Spathia (their spiritual double), with which the relationship is fateful. Women are attracted to men of the suit of Diamonds (especially if they are wealthy) and men of the suit of Cups. Men with this card often create friendships with women of the suit of Spathia.\n\n5. WORK AND MONEY\nThey achieve success in business and the material sphere, with partnership being a prerequisite for their progress. They should be cautious with documentation and maintain proper business papers. They have an affinity for rich and influential partners, but there is a risk of office romances and mixing work with personal emotions.\n\n6. KARMIC LESSON\nThe main task is to find a balance between high spiritual ideals of love and earthly reality. They must learn a practical approach to feelings and be careful not to use others emotionally. The lesson also includes overcoming pride through compromises in relationships.\n\n7. LIFE CYCLES\nMercury (0-13 years): A period of love and openness to all people.\nVenus (13-26 years): A desire to create their own activity and business; they often achieve success.\nMars (26-39 years): They need to tame their pride and learn to compromise and make concessions in relationships.\nJupiter (39-52 years): Accumulation of new knowledge and building a stable worldview.\nSaturn (52+ years): Finding a new partnership and opportunities for good profits."
