    "Text": "1. ARCHETYPE AND SYMBOLISM\nThe Ace of Cups represents the primordial “thirst for love” and the creative powers of the soul. As the first card in the deck, it carries the energy of a “young soul” – impulsive, searching for oneself, symbolizing the beginning of new relationships, the birth of feelings or children.\nCard number: 1\n\n2. STRENGTHS\nPeople with this birth card possess enormous creative and spiritual potential, often becoming famous writers or artists. They are masculine, valiant and courageous, which, combined with wisdom, helps them quickly reach the top. When they are calm and grateful to fate, they easily materialize their desires and achieve great financial success.\n\n3. CHALLENGES\nThe main obstacles facing them are egocentrism, indecision and inner restlessness, characteristic of odd cards. They tend to scatter their energy in many directions instead of following a specific plan, which leads to stress and dissatisfaction. The fear of lack of money and secret biases can divert them from the right path and block their development.\n\n4. LOVE AND RELATIONSHIPS\nIn their personal lives, they are in constant search of new love adventures and often change their partners, as they change their values ​​in the process of self-discovery. Their relationships are often marked by inconstancy and hesitation. To be happy, they need a partner who does not impose his presence and with whom they can share travels and experiences. Ace of Cups men like women of the suit of Diamonds. Women with this card get along well with Spathi men, and Spade men often see in them their ideal.\n\n5. WORK AND MONEY\nProfessional fulfillment requires variety and creativity; routine kills them. They are suitable for the field of art, literature and innovation. They have a strong need for financial stability (influence of Ace of Wands), but success comes only when they overcome the fear of poverty and develop a sense of gratitude for what they already have. They must learn to plan and act consistently.\n\n6. KARMIC LESSON\nThe main spiritual task is self-knowledge and understanding that love is an internal state, not something that is found outside. They must transform selfishness into love for themselves and others, as well as find peace in their soul, avoiding chaos and impermanence.\n\n7. LIFE CYCLES\nMercury (0-13 years): A period of strong focus on money and a desire to get rich.\nVenus (13-26 years): A time of happiness, love, creating a home and enjoying luxury and beautiful things.\nMars (26-39 years): A stage of reassessment of relationships, divorces, separations and travels are possible.\nJupiter (39-52): A period of creative upsurge, versatility of mind and attainment of wisdom.\nSaturn (52+): Possible occurrence of stress or engagement in several different activities at the same time."
